<section class="ip-section" id="rights-boundary" aria-labelledby="rights-boundary-heading">
  <div class="ip-section-heading">
    <h2 id="rights-boundary-heading">Customer-directed ownership, defined before development</h2>
    <p>Development ownership is confirmed as the customer directs. For joint development, once the agreed one-time development fee is paid in full, the project development results belong to the customer or the rights holder designated by the customer.</p>
  </div>
  <p>The project agreement identifies the intended rights holder, development scope, one-time development fee and deliverables. It also records the formats and arrangements for handing over files, tooling and technical information, so ownership and practical delivery are addressed together.</p>
  <div class="ip-table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Rights boundaries for project information and development results">
    <table class="ip-table">
      <caption>Separate the materials already owned from the results developed for the project.</caption>
      <thead>
        <tr><th scope="col">Category</th><th scope="col">Ownership and use</th><th scope="col">What to confirm</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><th scope="row">Customer's existing IP</th><td>Customer-provided ideas, designs, content, files and other IP remain with the customer or the relevant rights holder. Access for project work does not authorize reuse elsewhere.</td><td>What is provided, who may use it and the permitted project purpose.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">New project development results</th><td>The customer directs ownership. For joint development, the agreed project results belong to the customer or its designated rights holder once the agreed one-time development fee is paid in full.</td><td>The development scope, designated rights holder, agreed fee and handover obligations.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Third-party licensed content or technology</th><td>Any third-party material is identified and its applicable license terms are confirmed in advance. Its inclusion does not transfer rights beyond those terms.</td><td>The approved component or content, license permissions, restrictions and any required separate authorization.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="ip-section" id="handover-scope" aria-labelledby="handover-scope-heading">
  <div class="ip-section-heading">
    <h2 id="handover-scope-heading">Agree what will be delivered, in usable formats</h2>
    <p>The handover list is confirmed for the actual project. It identifies the files, physical items, approved versions, formats, recipient and delivery arrangements included in the agreed scope.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="ip-table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Development deliverables to confirm in the project scope">
    <table class="ip-table">
      <caption>Delivery categories are selected and documented for each project.</caption>
      <thead>
        <tr><th scope="col">Delivery category</th><th scope="col">Items to define in the handover list</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><th scope="row">Industrial and structural design</th><td>Approved industrial design, structural design, CAD models and drawings, with the agreed editable and exchange formats.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Tooling and technical information</th><td>Moulds and tooling within scope, their identification and location, associated tooling files, and the agreed technical documents and transfer arrangements.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Electronic design files</th><td>The agreed schematics, circuit-board design files, production documents and associated electronic information.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Programs and firmware</th><td>Approved programs, production firmware, encrypted packages and agreed source files, with their version and delivery format recorded.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Audio and other product content</th><td>The approved audio and content files developed or supplied for the project, subject to the confirmed rights and license terms.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Packaging files</th><td>Approved packaging designs, artwork and production files in the agreed formats.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p class="ip-note">Source code, production firmware and encrypted packages serve different purposes. Their delivery and manufacturing access are defined in the project scope. See <a href="/manufacturing/secure-programming/">secure programming and firmware protection</a> for the related release and production controls.</p>
</section>

<section class="ip-section" id="written-authorization" aria-labelledby="written-authorization-heading">
  <div class="ip-section-heading">
    <h2 id="written-authorization-heading">Project access is not permission for other uses</h2>
    <p>Customer materials, designs, samples and development results are used only for the authorized project. Without the customer's written authorization, they must not be:</p>
  </div>
  <ul class="ip-checklist">
    <li>Reused for another customer or an unrelated product.</li>
    <li>Resold, licensed or supplied to another party outside the authorized project scope.</li>
    <li>Disclosed beyond the people and approved external parties authorized to perform the project work.</li>
    <li>Shown publicly in a showroom, exhibition, website, social media post, photograph, video or other promotional material.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Approval to manufacture, inspect or subcontract a defined task does not by itself grant permission to publicize or otherwise exploit the customer's work. Any requested use outside the project purpose is discussed separately and requires written authorization.</p>
</section>
